  </data>
  <data name="DevicesPage_2.Message" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Starting it now… If this persists, reinstall DisplayMaster.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DevicesPage_3.Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Accept USB debugging on your device</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DevicesPage_3.Message" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Unlock the tablet or phone and tap Allow on the 'Allow USB debugging?' prompt.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DevicesPage_4.Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Extend mode needs the virtual display driver</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DevicesPage_4.Message" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Until it's installed, devices mirror your main screen.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DevicesPage_5.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>How to install</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DevicesPage_6.Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Running without administrator rights</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DevicesPage_6.Message" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Pen and touch can't reach apps running as administrator, and display settings may be read-only.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DevicesPage_7.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Restart as administrator</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DevicesPage_8.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Connect a tablet or phone</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DevicesPage_9.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Install DisplayMaster on the Android device, then pick a way to connect.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DevicesPage_10.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>USB (fastest)</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DevicesPage_11.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>1. Turn on USB debugging in Developer options.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DevicesPage_12.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>2. Plug the device into this PC.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DevicesPage_13.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>3. That's it: the app opens and connects by itself.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DevicesPage_14.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Wi-Fi</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DevicesPage_15.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>1. Allow Wi-Fi connections on the Connection page.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DevicesPage_16.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>2. In the app, enter this PC's address:</value>
  </data>
