  <data name="PenPage_1.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Pen &amp; Touch</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PenPage_2.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Applies to every connected device, immediately.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PenPage_3.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Pressure</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PenPage_4.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ignore light pressure below</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PenPage_5.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Stops accidental marks when the pen barely touches the screen.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PenPage_6.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Full pressure at</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PenPage_7.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Lower it to reach the thickest stroke without pressing hard.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PenPage_8.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Feel</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PenPage_9.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Softer</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PenPage_10.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Firmer</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PenPage_11.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Reset to default</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PenPage_12.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Light</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PenPage_13.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Pen pressure</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PenPage_14.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Hard</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PenPage_15.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Works with</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PenPage_16.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Pressure, tilt, hover and the pen's side button reach apps through Windows Ink: Photoshop, Krita, Clip Studio Paint, OneNote, Illustrator, Blender and more. The side button acts as right-click; the eraser end erases in apps that support it.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PenPage_17.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>On the device, pick how fingers behave from the quick panel (swipe in from the right edge): Touch, Mouse or Trackpad. While the pen is near the screen, touches are ignored so your palm can rest on it.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ConnectionPage_1.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Connection</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ConnectionPage_2.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>USB</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ConnectionPage_3.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Lowest latency and no network setup. Plug in a device with USB debugging enabled and it connects automatically.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ConnectionPage_4.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ready over USB: </value>
  </data>
  <data name="ConnectionPage_5.Message" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Android platform-tools (adb) weren't found, so USB connections are off. Reinstall DisplayMaster or install platform-tools.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ConnectionPage_6.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Wi-Fi</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ConnectionPage_7.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Connect without a cable on the same network. Use 5 GHz Wi-Fi for the best experience. Only turn this on for networks you trust.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ConnectionPage_8.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Nearby devices find this PC automatically. You can also enter this address in the app:</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ConnectionPage_9.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Phone doesn't have the app yet?</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ConnectionPage_10.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Scan this with the phone's camera to download it from this PC, then open the file to install. Android may ask you to allow installs from your browser once.</value>
